card.statement:
Let $\mc A$ be a $\zeta $-adjoint operator on a vector space $V$ with nondegenerate $\varepsilon$-Hermitian form $\mc F$ over a field $\ff$ of characteristic different from $2$ with involution, where $\varepsilon,\zeta \in\{1,-1\}$ and $\varepsilon= 1$ for nonidentity involution on $\ff$ (see <<ref:jna>>). Then there exists a basis of\/ $V$ in which the pair $(\mc A,\mc  F)_V$ is given by a direct sum of matrix pairs of the following types:

- [(i)] $A^{f(x)}_{\Phi}:=(\Phi,
\Phi_{\varepsilon\zeta}f(\Phi))$, in which $\Phi\in \mc O_{\ff}$ is a matrix for which $\Phi_{\varepsilon\zeta}$ exists, $0\ne
f(x)=\ba f(\zeta x)\in \ff[x]$, and $\deg(f(x))<\deg(p_{\Phi}(x))$.

- [(ii)] $\left(\mat{\Phi&0\\ 0&\zeta \Phi^{*}},\mat{
0&\varepsilon I_n\\I_n&0}\right)$, in which $\Phi\in \mc O_{\ff}$ is a matrix for which $\Phi_{\varepsilon\zeta}$ does not exist.

The summands are determined to the following extent:

- [Type (i)] up to replacement of the whole group of summands $
A_{\Phi}^{f_1(x)}
\oplus\dots\oplus
A_{\Phi}^{f_s(x)}
$ with the same $\Phi$ by $
A_{\Phi}^{g_1(x)}
\oplus\dots\oplus
  A_{\Phi}^{g_s(x)}
$ such that the Hermitian forms

\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&f_1(\omega)x_1^{\circ}x_1+\dots+
f_s(\omega)x_s^{\circ}x_s,
\\
&g_1(\omega)x_1^{\circ}x_1+\dots+
g_s(\omega)x_s^{\circ}x_s
\end{split}
\end{equation}

are equivalent over the field

\begin{equation}
\ff[\omega]=\ff[x]/p_{\Phi}(x)\ff[x]\text{ with involution } f(\omega)\mapsto
f(\omega)^{\circ}= \ba
f(\zeta \omega).
\end{equation}

- [Type (ii)] up to replacement of $\Phi$ by $\Psi\in \mc O_{\ff}$ with $\chi_{\Psi}(x)
=\zeta^{\deg(\chi_{\Psi})}\ba\chi_{\Phi}(\zeta x)$.
